            <div xml:id="d360">

                <pb facs="0460" n="450" sameAs="frus:frus1947v07/pg450"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">894A.00/4–1747: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Stuart</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-04-17">April 17,
                        1947</date>.<lb/>[Received April 17—3:11 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>830. At regular weekly Ministry of Information press conference April 16, when
                    questioned as to whether or not President Chiang Kaishek approved
                    recommendations submitted by General Pai Chunghsi on the reform of Taiwan,
                    Minister Peng Hsueh-pei said that the recommendations of General Pai have been
                    submitted to the President and are under consideration now. The Minister said he
                    was sure most of the suggestions will be accepted and that prompt action will be
                    taken to carry them out.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stuart</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
